bility=0 at load 0.3; it did not establish edibility.\\\",\\\"Keep the remaining 0.9 hazelnut separate from known-safe meals. Current satiety is 93.2 and energy 39.5, so immediate feeding or recovery is unnecessary.\\\",\\\"Evaluate the returned implementation and its limitations before committing materials or learning time.\\\"],\\\"preferences\\\":[\\\"Prefer capabilities with a real practical effect over interfaces that only label or observe an unsupported process.\\\",\\\"Use roots and berries for food while hazelnut toxicity and nutrition remain unresolved.\\\"],\\\"projects\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"local-food-evidence\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"paused\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"What nearby food reserves can be used safely, and what can physical tests establish about an unfamiliar hazelnut?\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"At tick 32, inventory contains three roots, five berries and 0.9 hazelnut.\\\",\\\"Personal knowledge lists root nutrition 14 and berry nutrition 8, both with toxicity 0.\\\",\\\"The tick-32 physical press trial consumed 0.1 hazelnut and measured load 0.3, held=true and flexibility=0.\\\",\\\"The trial confirmed a mechanical property; no hazelnut nutrition or toxicity result was reported.\\\"],\\\"uncertainty\\\":\\\"Hazelnut nutrition and toxicity remain unknown. The reported press result applies only to the tested load condition.\\\",\\\"goal\\\":\\\"Maintain known-safe reserves and distinguish measured properties from unresolved food-safety questions.\\\",\\\"completedSteps\\\":[\\\"Collected a hazelnut sample.\\\",\\\"Requested an assessment method and received the existing probe interface.\\\",\\\"Performed a low-intensity press trial on 0.1 hazelnut.\\\"],\\\"outputs\\\":[\\\"Verified hazelnut load-response observation at load 0.3.\\\",\\\"Remaining owned hazelnut sample of 0.9 unit.\\\"],\\\"missing\\\":\\\"A supported way to establish hazelnut food safety.\\\",\\\"next\\\":\\\"Revisit only if a suitable safety-assessment method becomes available; do not infer safety from mechanical tests.\\\",\\\"pauseReason\\\":\\\"Further mechanical testing does not answer the current food-safety question.\\\",\\\"benefit\\\":\\\"A previously unknown mechanical property was confirmed; known-safe roots and berries remain available.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"functional-food-preservation\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"active\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"Can a supported physical process actually slow decay of known-safe food?\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"Owned roots and berries have accumulated decay.\\\",\\\"The controlled-food-processing-trial interface explicitly states that ground exposure does not preserve food or extend its lifetime.\\\"],\\\"uncertainty\\\":\\\"A functional preservation method, its required resources and its costs are not yet known.\\\",\\\"goal\\\":\\\"Identify a practical, measurable means of reducing food losses without assuming unsupported effects.\\\",\\\"completedSteps\\\":[],\\\"outputs\\\":[],\\\"missing\\\":\\\"A supported preservation mechanism and exact operational requirements.\\\",\\\"next\\\":\\\"Request a functional method, then assess the response before undertaking work.\\\",\\\"pauseReason\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"benefit\\\":\\\"No preservation benefit has been established.\\\"}]}\"}","logprobs":[]}

