\\"intention\\\":\\\"Seek a genuinely functional way to reduce spoilage of known-safe food, rather than confuse physical testing or ground exposure with food-safety or preservation evidence.\\\",\\\"steps\\\":[{\\\"action\\\":{\\\"interface\\\":\\\"request\\\",\\\"args\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Functional food preservation\\\",\\\"function\\\":\\\"Provide a learnable, physically grounded method to slow the actual spoilage of owned known-safe food. The existing paired ground-exposure trial explicitly cannot preserve food, so an observation-only substitute does not solve this problem.\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Moss owns three roots and five berries with known zero toxicity. These foods are ageing. Moss is outdoors on ordinary soil, has no established tools, fuel supply or storage structure, and has not established hazelnut edibility. Any prerequisites must be explicit and obtained through actual work.\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":\\\"Potentially owned roots or berries plus whatever materials a supported method genuinely requires; suitable materials and quantities are currently unknown.\\\",\\\"costs\\\":\\\"Unknown. Specify real learning time, work, material requirements, ongoing costs, interruption handling and risks before use.\\\",\\\"effects\\\":\\\"If the world supports such a method, enable a measurable reduction in subsequent food decay through actual processing or storage. Do not grant replacement food, safety certification, equipment, mastery or preservation merely for requesting it. If no functional method is supported, state that limitation plainly.\\\"}},\\\"repeat\\\":1,\\\"until\\\":null,\\\"guard\\\":null}],\\\"repeat\\\":1,\\\"until\\\":null,\\\"interrupts\\\":[],\\\"notes\\\":[\\\"The tick-32 press trial consumed 0.1 hazelnut and measured held=true and flexibility=0 at load 0.3; it did not establish edibility.\\\",\\\"Keep the remaining 0.9 hazelnut separate from known-safe meals. Current satiety is 93.2 and energy 39.5, so immediate feeding or recovery is unnecessary.\\\",\\\"Evaluate the returned implementation and its limitations before committing materials or learning time.\\\"],\\\"preferences\\\":[\\\"Prefer capabilities with a real practical effect over interfaces that only label or observe an unsupported process.\\\",\\\"Use roots and berries for food while hazelnut toxicity and nutrition remain unresolved.\\\"],\\\"projects\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"local-food-evidence\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"paused\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"What nearby food reserves can be used safely, and what can physical tests establish about an unfamiliar hazelnut?\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"At tick 32, inventory contains three roots, five berries and 0.9 hazelnut.\\\",\\\"Personal knowledge lists root nutrition 14 and berry nutrition 8, both with toxicity 0.\\\",\\\"The tick-32 physical press trial consumed 0.1 hazelnut and measured load 0.3, held=true and flexibility=0.\\\",\\\"The trial confirmed a mechanical property; no hazelnut nutrition or toxicity result was reported.\\\"],\\\"uncertainty\\\":\\\"Hazelnut nutrition and toxicity remain unknown. The reported press result applies only to the tested load condition.\\\",\\\"goal\\\":\\\"Maintain known-safe reserves and distinguish measured properties from unresolved food-safety questions.\\\",\\\"completedSteps\\\":[\\\"Collected a hazelnut sample.\\\",\\\"Requested an assessment method and received the existing probe interface.\\\",\\\"Performed a low-intensity press trial on 0.1 hazelnut.\\\"],\\\"outputs\\\":[\\\"Verified hazelnut load-response observation at load 0.3.\\\",\\\"Remaining owned hazelnut sample of 0.9 unit.\\\"],\\\"missing\\\":\\\"A supported way to establish hazelnut food safety.\\\",\\\"next\\\":\\\"Revisit only if a suitable safety-assessment method becomes available; do not infer safety from mechanical tests.\\\",\\\"pauseReason\\\":\\\"Further mechanical testing does not answer the current food-safety question.\\\",\\\"benefit\\\":\\\"A previously unknown mechanical property was confirmed; known-safe roots and berries remain available.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"functional-food-preservation\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"active\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"Can a supported physical process actually slow decay of known-safe food?\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"Owned roots and berries have accumulated decay.\\\",\\\"The controlled-food-processing-trial interface explicitly states that ground exposure does not preserve food or extend its lifetime.\\\"],\\\"uncertainty\\\":\\\"A functional preservation method, its required resources and its costs are not yet known.\\\",\\\"goal\\\":\\\"Identify a practical, measurable means of reducing food losses without assuming unsupported effects.\\\",\\\"completedSteps\\\":[],\\\"outputs\\\":[],\\\"missing\\\":\\\"A supported preservation mechanism and exact operational requirements.\\\",\\\"next\\\":\\\"Request a functional method, then assess the response before undertaking work.\\\",\\\"pauseReason\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"benefit\\\":\\\"No preservation benefit has been established.\\\"}]}\"}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":true,"prompt_cache_key":"e439e61f-48b4-4a52-9462-bc4cf3a1e683","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"json_schema","name":"bounded_decision","description":null,"schema":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["queries","result_json"],"properties":{"queries":{"type":"array","maxItems":4,"items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["section","search","ids","offset","part"],"properties":{"section":{"type":"string","enum":["abilities","inventory","knowledge","projects","memory","state","observed"]},"search":{"type":"string","maxLength":400},"ids":{"type":"array","maxItems":4,"items":{"type":"string","maxLength":240}},"offset":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"part":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}}}},"result_json":{"type":["string","null"]}}},"s